    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d911">

                <pb facs="0774" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Stuart, J. Leighton: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-24T17:00:00+08:00">June 24, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 24—10:27 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1371. I have had word indirectly from Chen Ming-shu that he has already had
                    conversations with Mao Tse-tung<anchor n="64" xml:id="d911-f1"/> and Chou En-lai
                    which he regards as completely satisfactory. He reports that he will hasten his
                    return to Shanghai via Nanking and expresses hope that I will delay my departure
                    for US accordingly (see Embtel 1322, June 18). Further comment will be made
                    after I have heard directly from Chen but I consider it significant that he saw
                    these two top Communist leaders so promptly and advanced date return south with
                    their approval.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d911-f1" n="64" xml:id="d911-f1-content">
                <p>Chairman of the Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
